// ─── Things Sam owns ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//
// An asset is one identified thing. What it cost, what improved it and what
// has been depreciated are its own history. `why condo` tells that history,
// and a sale realizes against it. Nobody writes a basis by hand, and there is
// no `.basis`: a payment `: improvement of condo` joins the condo, and a
// payment `: repair of condo` is spent.

/// The condo at 41 Alma St. It was bought on 2024-02-20 and has been rented out
/// since March 2024.
asset condo : rental-home
  in-service 2024-03-01        // ▸ `us/rental` depreciates it over 27.5 years, mid-month
  land       120_000 USD       // the part of its cost that is land, which is never depreciated

/// The studio's laptop. It arrives in the journal on 2026-01-24.
asset laptop : equipment
  owner studio                 // ▸ `us` expenses it in 2026 (§179), unless the studio elects otherwise
